.TH AX25 3 "2024-10-20" "libax25" "Linux Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
.BR ax25_aton ", " ax25_aton_entry ", " ax25_aton_arglist ", " ax25_ntoa ", " ax25_cmp ", " ax25_validate
\- AX.25 Address manipulation routines
.PP
.BR ax25 ", " netrom ", " rose ", " axports
\- AX.25 kernel interface and configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <netax25/ax25.h>
.B #include <netax25/axlib.h>
.PP
.BI "int ax25_aton(const char *" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
.BI "int ax25_aton_entry(const char *" cp ", char *" axp ");"
.BI "int ax25_aton_arglist(const char **" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
.BI "char *ax25_ntoa(ax25_address *" axp ");"
.BI "int ax25_cmp(ax25_address *" ax1 ", ax25_address *" ax2 ");"
.BI "int ax25_validate(char *" axp ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page describes the kernel AX.25 socket interface as provided
by the Linux kernel and the address manipulation routines provided by
libax25.
.PP
The kernel AX.25 interface is accessed via AF_AX25 sockets.  The
configuration of ports is described in \fBaxports\fR(5) and managed via
the libax25 configuration API documented in \fBlibax25_config\fR(3).
.SH "KERNEL AX.25 SOCKET INTERFACE"
.PP
The AF_AX25 address family provides the standard Linux kernel AX.25
network stack.  Sockets are created with:
.nf
.BI "int s = socket(AF_AX25, SOCK_SEQPACKET, 0);"
.fi
.PP
The address structure is \fBstruct sockaddr_ax25\fR:
.nf
.ft C
struct sockaddr_ax25 {
    sa_family_t sax25_family;      /* AF_AX25 */
    ax25_address sax25_call;       /* callsign */
    int          sax25_ndigis;     /* number of digipeaters */
    ax25_address sax25_digi[8];    /* digipeater addresses */
};
.ft R
.fi
.PP
The \fBax25_address\fR type is a 7-byte array representing an AX.25
callsign in shifted format (each byte is the APRS/AX.25 shifted ASCII
character).
.SH "SOCKET OPTIONS (SOL_AX25)"
The following options are available at level \fBSOL_AX25\fR (257):
.TP
.BR AX25_WINDOW
Window size (default 2)
.TP
.BR AX25_T1
T1 timeout in 100ms units (default 10)
.TP
.BR AX25_T2
T2 timeout in 100ms units (default 30)
.TP
.BR AX25_T3
T3 timeout in 100ms units (default 300)
.TP
.BR AX25_N2
Maximum retries (default 10)
.TP
.BR AX25_BACKOFF
Backoff algorithm (0=linear, 1=exponential)
.TP
.BR AX25_EXTSEQ
Extended sequence numbers (0=standard, 1=extended)
.TP
.BR AX25_PIDINCL
Include PID in received frames (0=no, 1=yes)
.TP
.BR AX25_IDLE
Idle timeout in seconds
.TP
.BR AX25_PACLEN
Maximum packet length
.TP
.BR AX25_IPMAXQUEUE
Maximum IP queue length
.TP
.BR AX25_IAMDIGI
Act as digipeater (0=no, 1=yes)
.TP
.BR AX25_KILL
Kill connection (value is port index)
.SH "IOCTL COMMANDS"
The following ioctls are available on AF_AX25 sockets:
.TP
.B SIOCAX25GETUID
Get UID associated with socket
.TP
.B SIOCAX25ADDUID
Add UID to socket
.TP
.B SIOCAX25DELUID
Delete UID from socket
.TP
.B SIOCAX25NOUID
Remove all UIDs from socket
.TP
.B SIOCAX25BPQADDR
Set BPQ Ethernet address
.TP
.B SIOCAX25GETPARMS
Get link parameters
.TP
.B SIOCAX25SETPARMS
Set link parameters
.TP
.B SIOCAX25OPTRT
Optimize routing
.TP
.B SIOCAX25CTLCON
Control connection (connect/disconnect)
.TP
.B SIOCAX25GETINFO
Get connection info
.TP
.B SIOCAX25ADDFWD
Add forward
.TP
.B SIOCAX25DELFWD
Delete forward
.SH "ADDRESS MANIPULATION (axlib.h)"
The functions in \fB<netax25/axlib.h>\fR provide address manipulation:
.TP
.BI "int ax25_aton_entry(const char *" cp ", char *" axp ");"
Convert ASCII callsign (e.g. "DB0ABC-1") to 7-byte network format.
Returns 0 on success, -1 on error.
.TP
.BI "void ax25_aton_entry_or_exit(const char *" cp ", char *" axp ");"
Like \fBax25_aton_entry()\fR but exits on error.
.TP
.BI "int ax25_aton(const char *" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
Parse address string with optional digipeaters.  Format:
\fIcallsign\fR [\fIVia\fR \fIcallsign\fR...].
.TP
.BI "void ax25_aton_or_exit(const char *" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
Like \fBax25_aton()\fR but exits on error.
.TP
.BI "int ax25_aton_arglist(const char **" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
Parse NULL-terminated array of strings as address with digipeaters.
.TP
.BI "void ax25_aton_arglist_or_exit(const char **" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
Like \fBax25_aton_arglist()\fR but exits on error.
.TP
.BI "char *ax25_ntoa(ax25_address *" axp ");"
Convert network-format address to ASCII (e.g. "DB0ABC-1").  Returns
pointer to static buffer (overwritten on subsequent calls).
.TP
.BI "int ax25_cmp(ax25_address *" ax1 ", ax25_address *" ax2 ");"
Compare two addresses.  Returns 0 if identical, 1 if different,
2 if only SSIDs differ.
.TP
.BI "int ax25_validate(char *" axp ");"
Validate ASCII callsign.  Returns \fBTRUE\fR (1) if valid, \fBFALSE\fR (0)
if not.
.TP
.BI "char *ax25_ntoa(ax25_address *" axp ");"
Convert network address to ASCII.  Static buffer, not thread-safe.
.TP
.BI "int ax25_cmp(ax25_address *" ax1 ", ax25_address *" ax2 ");"
Compare addresses.  Returns 0=identical, 1=different, 2=SSID-only diff.
.TP
.BI "int ax25_validate(char *" axp ");"
Validate callsign format.  Returns TRUE (1) or FALSE (0).
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.BR ax25_aton () and \fBax25_aton_arglist()\fR return -1 on error,
otherwise length of structure.
.PP
.BR ax25_aton_entry () returns -1 on error, 0 on success.
.PP
.BR ax25_cmp () returns 0 (identical), 1 (different), 2 (SSID only).
.PP
.BR ax25_validate () returns TRUE (1) or FALSE (0).
